- Liability exclusions: Specifies when certain parties involved in the offer are not liable for participant losses arising from misleading or deceptive statements, including where they:
  - Conducted reasonable inquiries and reasonably believed statements were not misleading;
  - Lacked knowledge that a statement was misleading;
  - Reasonably relied on information from specified third parties (non-directors/employees/agents);
  - Publicly withdrew consent to being named in the document (for specified roles);
  - Were unaware of new circumstances arising after the document was prepared.
- Australia notifications:
  - Tax: The plan is intended to be subject to Subdivision 83A-C of the Income Tax Assessment Act 1997.
  - Exchange control: Reporting may be required for cash transactions over set thresholds and for international transfers; an assisting Australian bank may report on the participant’s behalf, otherwise the participant must. Participants should seek personal advice on compliance.
- Austria notifications:
  - Exchange control: Possible annual reporting to the Austrian National Bank for securities held outside Austria via “Standmeldung/Wertpapiere,” with exemptions below thresholds and filings due by the 15th after each quarter.
  - Additional reporting may be required when shares are sold or dividends paid if cash is held abroad, including monthly reporting of foreign cash account movements and balances via “Meldungen SI-Forderungen und/oder SI-Verpflichtungen” when thresholds are exceeded.
